<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="052" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Azure OpenAI: re-test ADR-028 exception E-2, custom subdomain first (FR-E3)</title>
    <phase>5 Group 2</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag; touches an ADR exception registry entry.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Documented root cause with a specific first check.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>auth,bff-api,ai,api-key,adr</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>ADR-028 exception E-2 records that Azure OpenAI returns 401 under managed identity. Microsoft documents the usual root cause as a MISSING CUSTOM SUBDOMAIN — regional endpoints reject Entra tokens. Check that first; if it is the cause, this may be a one-config-change elimination.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer.</role>
  <goal>Either the key is cleared and MI works, or E-2 is re-affirmed with current evidence rather than inherited assumption.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>AiModule.cs:115,122-128 selects ApiKeyCredential when the key is set, else the DI TokenCredential — so clearing the key restores MI in one config change IF the underlying 401 is fixed. Research established the documented causes: missing custom subdomain, missing Cognitive Services OpenAI User role, and up to 5 minutes of role propagation.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AiModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="none" status="complete">Independent</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: CHECK THE CUSTOM SUBDOMAIN FIRST on spaarke-openai-dev before anything else. It is the documented root cause of exactly this symptom.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: allow up to 5 minutes for role propagation before concluding MI does not work.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: if MI still fails, RE-AFFIRM E-2 with current evidence and a dated note. Do not leave it standing on a stale assumption — that is the failure mode this project exists to fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: .claude/adr edits are main-session only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Azure OpenAI, Entra auth, custom subdomains</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/RESEARCH-FINDINGS.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Check whether spaarke-openai-dev has a custom subdomain configured.</step>
    <step>Verify the UAMI holds Cognitive Services OpenAI User on the account.</step>
    <step>Clear the key in a non-production context and test inference under MI, allowing for propagation.</step>
    <step>If it works, clear the key and update E-2 to resolved.</step>
    <step>If it fails, capture the exact error and re-affirm E-2 with dated current evidence.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Adding a custom subdomain would change the endpoint URL consumers depend on — STOP; that is a breaking change beyond this task's scope.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/052-openai-e2-retest.md</output>
    <output type="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The custom-subdomain hypothesis is explicitly tested and the result recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion>Either the key is cleared and inference works under MI, or E-2 carries dated current evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: E-2 is NOT left standing on the original stale assumption under any outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: no consumer-visible endpoint URL changed.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
